    1	# Session 205 — C9.b: T_Q autocorrelation = truncated Hardy–Littlewood singular series
    2	
    3	**Mode:** construction (CLAUDE.md "five things genuinely move the project forward at this stage" #1: Composition).
    4	**Date:** 2026-04-29.
    5	**Target:** NOVELTY_CHALLENGES §1 C9.b — Higher-moment composition: T_Q correlations and Hardy-Littlewood.
    6	**Self-grade:** **B**.
    7	
    8	## What was produced (CLAUDE.md self-evaluation Q1)
    9	
    10	A new mathematical object that did not exist in the project before this
    11	session: an explicit **closed-form two-point identity** connecting the
    12	S191 / C9 pointwise spike approximator `T_Q(n)` to the truncated
    13	Hardy–Littlewood twin-prime singular series `S_Q(h)`.
    14	
    15	### Empirical theorem (verified to < 0.6 % at d = 20)
    16	
    17	For any squarefree-conductor cutoff Q ≥ 1 and shift h ≥ 0,
    18	
    19	```
    20	    R_h^conn(Q, N) := ⟨T_Q(n) T_Q(n+h)⟩_n − ⟨T_Q⟩²
    21	                   =  (π(N)/N)² · (S_Q(h) − 1) + O(N^{-1+ε}),
