    827:| §D48 ATTACK_VECTORS — Bost-Connes endomotive Galois orbits of χ_P-projected KMS_∞ ground states (CCM 2007 *Adv. Math.* 214, 761 = arXiv:math/0512138 §6.2): does the abelian Hilbert-12 Galois action on χ_P-projected pure ground states of the truncated BC algebra carry detectable prime-distribution content beyond Dirichlet equidistribution? (cross-domain: Bost-Connes 1995 *Selecta Math.* 1, 411; CCM 2007 endomotive formalism; Connes-Marcolli 2008 textbook; Marcolli 2005 *Arithmetic Noncommutative Geometry*) | FAIL | E | S203 wild-swing single-session attack on the S163-flagged "highest-A-prior open vector". Closes at mode E (matched-density null) across 14 moduli `N ∈ {30, 60, 90, 105, 120, 210, 330, 420, 510, 630, 840, 1155, 1260, 2310}`. **Construction**: truncate the BC C*-algebra to its commutative sub `\mathcal{A}_N := \mathbb{C}[(\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z})^*]`; pure KMS_∞ ground states `\phi_\omega(\delta_a) = \omega(a)` parametrised by characters `\omega \in \widehat{G}`, `G = (\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z})^*`. Define χ_P-projector `P_\chi := Σ_{p ≤ N \text{ prime}, \gcd(p,N)=1} δ_p`; projected functional on the corner reduces to `ω(P_\chi)² · ω(a)`. Two characters give equal projected functionals iff `ω = ω'` or both `ω(P_\chi) = ω'(P_\chi) = 0`; the **zero set** `Z_\chi := {ω : S_\chi(ω) := Σ_p ω(p) = 0}` defines a single merged eq-class. Cyclotomic Galois `(\mathbb{Z}/M\mathbb{Z})^*` (`M = exp G`) acts via `σ_a · ω = ω^a` — Hilbert-12 action restricted to truncation. **Empirics**: `n_zero(χ)` measured against 50-trial random matched-density null `R ⊂ G` with `|R| = |P_N|`. `|z(n_zero)| ≤ 1.1` at every N. Per-bin orbit-length z-scores (14 N × 4–5 bins ≈ 65 tests): max `|z| = 3.39` at `N=60` length-1 bin (a confirmed finite-size artefact — residues `1, 49 mod 60` lack any prime ≤ 60, smallest are 61 and 109; anomaly disappears at `N=120` once these primes fill in); two single-bin `|z| > 3` deviations expected by chance. **No 5σ deviation, no consistent direct