ingle rank-1 component with eigenvalue ≈ `α · N`, `α = (1/N)Σ ε(k)(−1)^k ≈ 1/√log N`. After BDJ scaling, `λ̃_max ≈ √(N/log N)`. By Szegő (Grenander-Szegő), `m_4 ≈ (1/2π)∫f^4 dθ / N²` and `(1/2π)∫|F_N|^4 dθ` is the **Hardy-Littlewood additive energy of primes**, with leading scaling `2N · π(N)²/log²N` from Goldbach-style major arcs. **Adds EDGE E2.31** (the L^k generalisation of E2.21 from L^∞ point evaluation to L^k integral evaluation, accessed via Szegő-Toeplitz spectral moments framed in the BDJ free-probability universality framework). Distinct from CLOSED line 690 (R-transform of `diag(1_P)`, trivial idempotent ESD = (1−π(N)/N)δ_0 + (π(N)/N)δ_1, encoded only π(N) — Toeplitz/Hankel here MIXES χ_P at all offsets producing non-trivial continuous spectrum). Distinct from S74-S168 chain (MPS-Gram model with MP bulk + spike outliers k* ~ R^{0.85}; here raw χ_P gives single parity outlier q=2). Distinct from E2.21 (point evaluation at single rationals; here L^k integrals). **Cross-domain ingredient**: BDJ free-probability framework — appended to `CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md` §3 as "Bryc-Dembo-Jiang Toeplitz/Hankel universal LSD" USED-I. **Falsifier**: any (N, kind, k) cell with empirical `m_k(χ_P)` matching BDJ universal limit within ±2σ — empirically falsified across 32 cells × moments. OR exhibition of a polylog computational extraction of `λ_max(χ_P-T, N) = (4/π)√(N/log N) = (4/π)√π(N)` as a primality witness — would resolve polylog π(x). **No algorithmic upside**: extracting λ_max of an N×N Toeplitz via Lanczos costs Ω(N log N) per matrix-vector multiply, same order as direct enumeration. **Successors proposed (S204)**: D3.a (Liouville Toeplitz/Hankel BDJ test — predicts FULL BDJ universality since Möbius cancellation kills the parity spike; this would sharpen E2.31 by exhibiting matched-density sequence with NO major-arc spike; the L^k generalisation of D27.b OPEN from S138, 1 session); D3.b (centered χ_P with parity bias subtracted Toeplitz BDJ — should match BDJ