    331:| Bourgain-Glibichuk-Konyagin sum-product gain on the prime set in F_p (ATTACK_VECTORS §D9) | FAIL | E | First sum-product / additive-combinatorial measurement of `A_prime ⊂ F_p` in the project. For p ∈ {1009, 10007, 100003, 1000003} and K_factor ∈ {0.5, 1.0, 1.5, 2.0} (10 cells, n_random=100; p=10⁶ at n_random=30): `\|A_prime · A_prime\|_Z = π(K)·(π(K)+1)/2` EXACTLY at every cell — primes are multiplicatively atomic by unique factorisation, no factor coincidences. Matched-parity-random subsets B ⊂ [3, K] ∪ {2} of cardinality \|A_prime\| have `\|B · B\|_Z < N(N+1)/2` by an O(N²/log K) divisor-coincidence rate, giving z-score scaling `z_p ≈ 1.0 (p=10³) → 2.2 (p=10⁴) → 3.4 (p=10⁵) → 6.0 (p=10⁶)` at K_factor=1.0 (`z ≈ 0.7 √(log p)` empirical fit). **Green-Tao W=6-tricked control (B4) does NOT reduce the multiplicative deviation** — z_p_B4 roughly equal to or slightly larger than z_p_B3 — confirming the mechanism is unique-factorisation atomicity, NOT coprime-to-6 sieving. The additive direction `\|A_prime + A_prime\|_p` matches B3 within +1.0..+1.5σ (sub-significant per cell, sustained across 10 cells); under W=6 trick (B4), drops to +0.5..+1.2σ, joining the existing W-trick fingerprint at E2.13/E2.19. **A-grade outcome FALSIFIED**: BGK gain has NO closed-form HL singular-series interpretation — the technique is structurally insensitive to HL-class structure on primes because the multiplicative side saturates trivially. **B-grade closure**: clean structural negative result + new shape edge **E2.32** (multiplicative-independence saturation as the bottleneck of BGK on primes; SEVENTH orthogonal HL/multiplicative-structure category after E2.13, E2.14, E2.15, E2.17, E2.19, E2.20, E2.21, E2.31). CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES §7 row "Sum-product theorems (Bourgain-Glibichuk-Konyagin in F_p)" PROPOSED → USED-E. **Channelled mathematician**: Tao. See `experiments/algebraic/sum_product_chi_p_BGK/`, `archive/sessions/session207_d9_bgk_sum_product.md`. | 207 |
